Conjugate Priors and the Role of Data

An exact, interactive Bayesian updating explorer for Normal-Normal (known
variance), Beta-Binomial, Gamma-Poisson, and Gamma-Gamma (known shape) models.
Gamma parameters use the shape-rate convention. The page runs entirely in
HTML/CSS/JavaScript with no Shiny, WebR, CDN, or runtime installation.

The controls specify sufficient statistics rather than simulated observations,
so changing the prior does not resample the data. Compare prior, normalised
likelihood, and posterior densities, posterior means and credible intervals,
and the influence of a fixed prior as sample size increases.

Open Conjugate/index.html directly, or serve the repository with any static
web server. Keep TeachingTools/ beside the tool folders when copying them:
statistics.js supplies shared probability functions and browser.js/browser.css
supply Canvas drawing and responsive styling. No build step is needed.

Run numerical and actual-browser checks (Node 22+, Chrome for browser tests):
  node --test TeachingTools/test_statistics.js Conjugate/test_conjugate.js
  node Conjugate/test_browser.js

The numerical checks include Bayes-product identities, sequential/batch
equivalence, boundary counts, fixed-data behavior and R-calibrated quantiles.
Browser tests cover all pairs, no-data states, prior/data presets, diagnostics,
keyboard tabs, mobile layout and offline file use. CHROME_BIN can select Chrome.

The original app.R and conjugate.R remain an R/Shiny reference, not part of
the served page. Their existing regression checks are retained:
  Rscript Conjugate/test_conjugate.R

Build the HTML tools for GitHub Pages:
  node deploy.js

html-tools.json lists the published tools and explicit local/shared assets.
The clean _site/ artifact contains no R payloads, editor pages, or Shiny/WebR
runtime. All twenty tools are now native HTML; R implementations remain reference
source and are not published.

Teaching reference:
https://anguswright.github.io/LectureNotes/IntroductionToStatistics_Section3b_html.html#conjugate-priors
